        {
          "id": "6a63a036326897f1020650ea",
          "question_number": 13,
          "question": "{H}_{2} {O}_{2} disproportionates into {H}_{2} {O} and {O}_{2} . The equivalent weight of {H}_{2} {O}_{2} in this reaction is",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "image": null,
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "34",
            "17",
            "68",
            "8.5"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "marking": {
            "correct": 4,
            "incorrect": -1
          },
          "explanation": "Explanation:- The equivalent weight is the molecular weight MM divided by the number of electrons exchanged per mole of reactant n . Equivalent weight =MM/n We require the moles of electrons, so let's use the ion-electron approach to balance the equation. Incorrect equation :- H2O2&rarr;H2O+O2 Reduction: 1&times;H2O2+2H++2e-&rarr;2H2O Oxidation: 1&times;H2O2&rarr;O2+2H++2e- Overall: 2H2O2&rarr;O2+2H2O The process requires the transfer of 2 mol of electrons, as we can see. Due to the fact that the reaction also contains 2 mol of H2 O2, the amount of electrons transported per mole of H2 O2 is n=2 mole-2 molH2O2=1 mol per mole electrons of H2 O2 &there4; Equivalent weight =MM/n =34.01 g1=34.01 g This is the required solution. Hence, the correct option is (1). i.e. 34"
        }
      ]
